# 49. COMMON MISCONCEPTIONS

### ❌ "WPA2 can be cracked instantly."

Wrong.

Password strength and configuration matter.

### ❌ "A handshake contains the Wi-Fi password."

Wrong.

It contains authentication/key-establishment information used for verification.

### ❌ "A captured handshake means the password is known."

Wrong.

A password recovery attempt still has to find a matching candidate.

### ❌ "Hidden SSID prevents attacks."

Wrong.

SSID hiding is not a substitute for encryption/authentication.

### ❌ "MAC filtering is strong security."

Wrong.

MAC addresses can be observed and spoofed.

